<article class="env-lemma" id="0CBQ">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CBQ">Lemma <span data-tag="0CBQ">41.21.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $D \subset X$ be a normal crossings divisor. If $f : Y \to X$ is a smooth morphism of schemes, then the pullback $f^*D$ is a normal crossings divisor on $Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      As $f$ is flat the pullback is defined by Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/02OO" data-tag="02OO">31.14.13</a> hence the statement makes sense. Let $q \in f^*D$ map to $p \in D$. Choose an étale morphism $U \to X$ whose image contains $p$ such that $D \times _ X U \subset U$ is a strict normal crossings divisor as in Definition <a href="/tag/0BSF" data-tag="0BSF">41.21.4</a>. Set $V = Y \times _ X U$. Then $V \to Y$ is étale as a base change of $U \to X$ (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GO" data-tag="02GO">29.37.4</a>) and the pullback $D \times _ X V$ is a strict normal crossings divisor on $V$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0CBP" data-tag="0CBP">41.21.3</a>. Thus we have checked the condition of Definition <a href="/tag/0BSF" data-tag="0BSF">41.21.4</a> for $q \in f^*D$ and we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>